    rLede: (): Part[] => [n(RF.nominal_folders), ' nominal participant folders watched the same ', n(RF.videos), ' videos: ', n(RF.clips), ' stored EEG clips, not as many independent people. For each clip the target is the mean of its stored valence and arousal ratings on the published raw scale from 1 to 255: descriptive self-report means, not SAM scores. Four fixed arms are scored by equal-axis mean absolute error, lower being better: EEG Ridge on relative band power at every channel position, and three controls that use no EEG — the training clips’ mean, the training target of the same video, and a ridge on stored duration and the numeric video ID. Two conditions: a folder held out with the videos shared (', n(shared.folds), ' folds), and a folder held out together with ', n(joint.held_clips_per_fold), ' of the videos it is tested on (', n(joint.folds), ' folds).'],
    rCaption: { shared: 'Equal-axis mean absolute error with the videos shared and a folder held out, raw label units: lower is better.', joint: 'Equal-axis mean absolute error with a folder and its test videos held out together, raw label units: lower is better.' },
    rLegend: 'Dot: the error over all clips of the condition; dashed line: the training-set mean’s error. No interval: two nominal folders support no population inference.',
    rRegion: 'REFED, equal-axis mean absolute error of the four arms in both conditions, scrolls horizontally',
    rTabCaption: (): Part[] => ['Equal-axis mean absolute error over the ', n(RF.clips), ' clips of each condition, in raw label units; lower is better. In the second condition the lookup finds a matching video for ', n(joint.lookup_matched_videos), ' of ', n(joint.clips_scored), ' clips, so it falls back to the training-set mean.'],
    colShared: 'Shared videos, a folder held out', colJoint: 'Folder and videos held out together', control: 'uses no EEG',
    rFindLabel: (): Part[] => ['EEG Ridge, equal-axis mean absolute error with the videos shared; the same-video lookup scores ', m3(SA.source_video_lookup.equal_axis_mae), ', the training-set mean ', m3(SA.source_global_mean.equal_axis_mae)],
    rFindH3: 'EEG band power has the largest error in both conditions',
    rFindP: (): Part[] => ['Held out together with the videos, EEG Ridge’s error is ', m3(JA.eeg_ridge.equal_axis_mae), ' against ', m3(JA.source_global_mean.equal_axis_mae), ' for the training-set mean. With shared videos, looking up the same video’s training target has the smallest error: a familiar stimulus carries the prediction through its identity, which is what that control is there to show. Held out together, the lookup has no matching video and equals the training-set mean. This illustrates the confound; it does not establish a mechanism.'],
    rLimits: 'Two nominal folders sharing their video keys: the clips are not independent people, so no interval or significance test is reported, and no population, cross-day or physiological claim follows. The rating arrays had been inspected and their means computed before this design, so these are not untouched targets. Stored EEG units, the EEG-to-rating clock and the crop end points are unresolved: published video durations exceed the stored arrays by two seconds, and pairing whole arrays establishes no precise alignment. The numeric video ID is a key index, not an established presentation order.',
    rSource: 'Data: Xiaojun Ning, Jing Wang, Zhiyang Feng, Tianzuo Xin, Shuo Zhang, Shaoqi Zhang, Zheng Lian, Yi Ding, Youfang Lin and Ziyu Jia,',
    rGated: 'gated.',
    rAudit: 'Independently audited: the sealed predictions reconstructed exactly, every metric recomputed independently and every preparation record verified. No raw signal or original annotation was reread, and no model was refitted.',
    // Not yet evaluated
    soEyebrow: 'Status only · no figure',
    soH2: 'Not yet evaluated',
    soLede: 'These analyses have not been run: the evidence a valid evaluation needs is missing, and none of them is a result.',
    // Methods and limits
    limitsH2: 'What these pilots can and cannot say',
    methodsH3: 'How each result was produced',
    methods: (): [string, Part[]][] => [
      ['Orthosis, classical features', ['The ', n(o64.signal.eeg_channels), ' EEG channels at ', n(o64.signal.sampling_hz), ' Hz with the declared header scaling, the recorded reference kept and the acceleration channels left out; continuous forward-only 1–30 Hz filtering that uses no future samples; the complete ', n(o64.signal.window_seconds[0]), '–', sec(o64.signal.window_seconds[1]), ' window (', n(o64.signal.window_samples), ' samples) after each event. ', n(o64.configuration.values_per_event), ' fixed amplitude and log band-power values per event (', n(o58.configuration.values_per_event), ' on the ', n(o58.signal.eeg_channels), ' channels), a training-only standardization and a balanced L2 logistic regression with C = 1, no tuning. Main-task runs only: ', n(C.exclusions.baseline_runs), ' baseline runs, ', n(C.exclusions.targets_without_following_movement), ' targets without a following movement and ', n(C.exclusions.windows_crossing_boundary), ' window crossing a boundary are left out, none depending on whether the person responded correctly. Every prediction was sealed before a separate scorer read the held-out labels.']],
      ['Orthosis, frozen EEGPT', ['The frozen ', n(M.encoder_parameters), '-parameter EEGPT target encoder at its native input of ', n(oep.encoder_input.channels), ' channels by ', n(oep.encoder_input.samples), ' samples: the same filtered window, resampled from ', n(oep.signal.sampling_hz), ' to ', n(oep.encoder_input.sampling_hz), ' Hz, microvolts divided by 1,000; its summary tokens, averaged over two temporal patches, feed the same probe. The encoder’s weights are unchanged: no fine-tuning and no LoRA. Across the ', n(oep.fits.folds), ' folds, ', n(oep.fits.fitted_probes), ' probes were fitted.']],
      ...(bingoReleased ? [['BINGO, inner speech', ['Per trial and channel, max-absolute scaling and demeaning, then Hann periodograms; four relative bands partition 1–30 Hz across the ', n(bingo.signal.channels), ' channels in source order, ', n(bingo.signal.values_per_trial), ' values per trial, with no voltage calibration, montage interpolation or re-referencing. A source-only standardization and a ridge classifier with fixed alpha 1. Controls: an order-only control, a high-frequency ratio control, the class prior and ', n(dirs[0].controls.label_shuffle.balanced_accuracy.replicates), ' training-label shuffles per direction; all ', n(bingo.fits.sealed_checkpoints), ' prediction checkpoints were sealed before scoring. One incomplete field is left out by a complete-record rule set before scoring. The protocol, from the project’s D3.1, version 2.0: the word is shown at ', sec(TL.word_shown), ', removed for a countdown at ', sec(TL.word_removed_countdown), ', and the fixation cross at ', sec(TL.fixation_inner_speech_onset), ' starts inner speech until ', sec(TL.end), '; ', n(bingo.protocol.nouns), ' nouns, ', n(bingo.protocol.repetitions_per_noun), ' repetitions each, in fully randomized order.']]] as [string, Part[]][] : []),
      ...(handwritingReleased ? [['Handwriting, mask-aware EEG', ['A fixed window 0.5–4.5 seconds after the released EEG-relative onset (4,000 samples at 1,000 Hz), read from the ', n(HV.channels_recorded), ' header-identified EEG channels only; the EOG, HECG and annotation channels and the optical samples are left out. Labels are the released event codes 200 to 203, mapped to 0 to 3. Before any transform, a channel-window is masked if it is constant, touches either header-declared digital rail or is not finite; the available channels are demeaned one by one, with no common-average reference and no interpolation. Welch spectra (1,000-sample Hann window, 500 overlap) give five half-open bands from 1 to 45 Hz, each divided by the sum of the five: 295 channel-major values per trial, zero where a channel is unavailable. Source-only standardization and a balanced multinomial logistic regression with C = 1, no tuning. The controls fit the same model on the availability bits and the available-channel fraction, on four elapsed-time and trial-order features, and on both. All 125 checkpoints, for 120 model fits and five majority controls, were sealed before a separate scorer read the held-out labels.']]] as [string, Part[]][] : []),
      ['REFED, stored clips', ['Five relative Welch band powers between 1 and 45 Hz, each divided by the channel’s total, at every channel position, with no channel selection or re-referencing; source-only standardization and Ridge with fixed alpha 1, no tuning, and predictions left unclipped. Every clip passed the numerical checks (', n(refed.quality.channel_clip_rows), ' channel–clip rows, ', n(refed.quality.clips_or_channels_removed), ' removed): finite, non-constant values and valid spectral denominators, which is numerical eligibility, not signal quality.']],
    ],
    intervalsH3: 'What the intervals cover',
    intervals: ['Orthosis: pointwise 95% percentile intervals from 10,000 person-level bootstrap draws, conditional on the sealed predictions; with eight people they are wide, and the paired interval resamples each person’s difference rather than comparing two separate intervals.',
      ...(bingoReleased ? ['BINGO: approximate descriptive intervals from 10,000 field bootstrap draws over overlapping leave-one-field-out fits; they omit refit variability and are not calibrated population confidence intervals.'] : []),
      ...(handwritingReleased ? ['Handwriting: descriptive 2.5–97.5% intervals from 10,000 fixed-seed person-bootstrap draws over the five people, conditional on the already fitted overlapping folds; they are not calibrated population confidence intervals and not evidence of superiority. Each bound is a percentile of resampled five-person means, not one person’s score; the mask-only control’s interval is not published, because its bounds would show individual people’s scores.'] : []),
      'REFED: none, because two nominal folders support no population inference.',
      bingoReleased || handwritingReleased ? 'The permutation and shuffle ranges are the lowest and highest replicate means, not intervals, and those controls are diagnostics, not significance tests.' : 'The permutation ranges are the lowest and highest replicate means, not intervals, and that control is a diagnostic, not a significance test.'].join(' '),
    limitsH3: heldPilots.length ? 'Limits that hold for every published pilot' : 'Limits that hold for all four',
